 34AL    9BE(36S,34AL)                 2012RO25                  ENSDF    202609
 34AL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2026$          
 34AL c  2012Ro25: a 600-pps, 93% pure {+34}Al secondary beam was produced via  
 34AL2c  the projectile fragmentation of a 77.5-MeV/nucleon {+36}S primary beam 
 34AL3c  on a 240-mg/cm{+2} {+9}Be target and selected by the LISE3 spectrometer
 34AL4c  at GANIL. {+34}Al ions were implanted into a 50-|mm Kapton foil in a   
 34AL5c  beam-on (120 ms)/beam-off (300 ms) mode. Electrons and positrons were  
 34AL6c  detected using four |DE-E telescopes, each consisting of a 1-mm-thick  
 34AL7c  Si detector and a 4.5-mm-thick Si(Li) detector. |g rays were detected  
 34AL8c  using two Ge clover detectors of the EXOGAM array. Measured E|b,       
 34AL9c  Ee{++}, Ee{+-}, E|g, |b|g-coin, and |be{++}/e{+-}coin. Deduced {+34}Al 
 34ALAc  g.s. and isomer T{-1/2}, {+34}Si levels, J, |p, transition strengths,  
 34ALBc  and configuration mixing. Comparisons with shell-model calculations.   
 34AL  L 0            4-               54.4 MS   5                              
 34AL cL J$from the Adopted Levels. Dominated by neutron 1p0h configuration     
 34AL2cL (f{-7/2}){+1} with a proton hole in d{-5/2} from shell-model           
 34AL3cL calculations (2012Ro25).                                               
 34AL cL T$from fit of |b decay curve in coincidence with 926-keV |b-delayed |g 
 34AL2cL ray in {+34}Si (2012Ro25).                                             
 34AL  L 46.7         1+               26 MS     1                           M  
 34AL cL E,J$from the Adopted Levels. E(level)=0.55 MeV and J|p=1+ with dominant
 34AL2cL neutron 2p1h configuration (d{-3/2}){+-1}(f{-7/2}){+2} from shell-model
 34AL3cL calculations (2012Ro25). A fit of |b decay curve in coincidence with   
 34AL4cL 3326-keV |b-delayed |g ray in {+34}Si yields a shorter T{-1/2} of 49.8 
 34AL5cL ms {I2}, which indicates that the 2+, 3326 level in {+34}Si is also fed
 34AL6cL by the |b decay of the isomer in {+34}Al. Even without decay branching 
 34AL7cL ratios, the fact that the both the 0+ and 2+ levels in {+34}Si are fed 
 34AL8cL by the isomer suggests a 1+ assignment for the isomer.                 
 34AL cL T$from fit of |b decay curve in coincidence with 511-keV |g ray arising
 34AL2cL from positron annihilation. The second 0+ state in {+34}Si is observed 
 34AL3cL to be populated by the |b decay of the 1+ isomer in {+34}Al and to     
 34AL4cL deexcite by E0 transition to 0+ g.s. of {+34}Si via the internal pair  
 34AL5cL formation (IPF). The sum energy of the electron-positron pair is       
 34AL6cL measured to be 1688 {I2} (2012Ro25).                                   
